From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:01:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: Force a mode set on a Colorspace
 change

The AVI infoframe, which carries the colorimetry, is only written on a
mode set, and a display engine in front of the controller may have to
convert into a different YCbCr encoding. A change of the Colorspace
property alone does not make the atomic helpers do a mode set, unlike
a max bpc change, so the new value would only take effect on the next
unrelated one. Mark the mode as changed, as is already done for the
HDR output metadata.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
index e3cd2acda..4e679b73a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi.c
@@ -2660,7 +2660,12 @@ static int dw_hdmi_connector_atomic_check(struct drm_connector *connector,
 	if (!crtc)
 		return 0;
 
-	if (!drm_connector_atomic_hdr_metadata_equal(old_state, new_state)) {
+	/*
+	 * The AVI infoframe colorimetry is only written on a mode set, and
+	 * the display engine may convert to a different YCbCr encoding.
+	 */
+	if (!drm_connector_atomic_hdr_metadata_equal(old_state, new_state) ||
+	    old_state->colorspace != new_state->colorspace) {
 		crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(state, crtc);
 		if (IS_ERR(crtc_state))
 			return PTR_ERR(crtc_state);
